  Th2HandbookHelp_AddAnchor("Chapter2#_table-223-msx-format-for-each-country_", 160)

  Th2HandbookHelp_Begin()
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("MSX has the escape sequence feature (see [Appendix 10](Appendices8and10.md#appendix-10---escape-sequences)), which can be used in the PRINT statement of BASIC, and in console output of BIOS or BDOS call (MSX-DOS). The escape sequence feature is a subset of DEC VT52 terminal and Heathkit H19 terminal.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_Commit("Escape sequence", "Chapter 2: BASIC")
  Th2HandbookHelp_AddAnchor("Chapter2#escape-sequence", 161)

  Th2HandbookHelp_Begin()
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("_Warm start_")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("After selecting a slot of MAIN-ROM, jump to 409BH of MAIN-ROM. If the work area of BASIC has not been destroyed, the BASIC prompt will be displayed. The contents of register and stack at the jump are ignored.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("Another way is to execute the next command in internal routine NEWSTT (see [4.4 of Chapter 2](Chapter2.md#44-expansion-of-cmd-command)) (see [[[Figure 2.20|||Chapter2#figure-220--input-setting-of-newstt-for-the-warm-start]]])")
  Th2HandbookHelp_Commit("Returning to BASIC", "Chapter 2: BASIC")
  Th2HandbookHelp_AddAnchor("Chapter2#returning-to-basic", 162)

  Th2HandbookHelp_Begin()
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("[[[[Ver Figura: Figure 2.20]|||img:figure_2.20]]]")
  Th2HandbookHelp_Commit("_Figure 2.20  Input setting of NEWSTT for the warm start_", "Chapter 2: BASIC")
  Th2HandbookHelp_AddAnchor("Chapter2#_figure-220-input-setting-of-newstt-for-the-warm-start_", 163)

  Th2HandbookHelp_Begin()
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("In the case of simple game cartridges which do not use the BIOS or BASIC work areas, the program can be invoked by writing a starting address for the program to " + Chr(34) + "INIT" + Chr(34) + " in ROM header. But using this method prevents the initial settings of another cartridge, so disk drives cannot be used.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("To prevent this, the hook " + Chr(34) + "H.STKE" + Chr(34) + " is at FEDAH; write the inter-slot call command in the program to be invoked at the execution on " + Chr(34) + "INIT" + Chr(34) + " routine of the cartridge, and return to the system by RET command. Then after initialising all cartridges and after preparing the DISK BASIC environment if there is a disk, the hook is called, so the objective program can be invoked. This method is also effective when there is no disk (see APPENDIX).")
  Th2HandbookHelp_Commit("Auto start", "Chapter 2: BASIC")
  Th2HandbookHelp_AddAnchor("Chapter2#auto-start", 164)

  Th2HandbookHelp_Begin()
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("Code  |  Message  |  Description")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("---  |  ---  |  ---")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("1  |  NEXT without FOR  |  There is no FOR statement corresponding with the NEXT statement.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("2  |  Syntax error  |  There is an error in syntax.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("3  |  RETURN without GOSUB  |  The RETURN statement does not correspond to the GOSUB statement.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("4  |  Out of DATA  |  There is no data to be READ by the READ statement.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("5  |  Illegal function call  |  There is an error in the function or numeric value specification.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("6  |  Overflow  |  The numeric value has overflow.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("7  |  Out of memory  |  The free area has been exhausted.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("8  |  Undefined line number  |  There is no such a line number in the program.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("9  |  Subscript out of range  |  The subscript value of the array variable exceeds the declared range.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("10  |  Redimensioned array  |  The array is declared twice.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("11  |  Division by zero  |  The attempt to divide by zero is made. The negative exponent of zero is done.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("12  |  Illegal direct  |  The statement which cannot be executed in the direct mode is carried out directly.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("13  |  Type mismatch  |  There is a conflict in the data types.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("14  |  Out of string space  |  The string space is exhausted.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("15  |  String too long  |  The length of the string is longer than 255 characters.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("16  |  String formula too complex  |  The specified string is too complex.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("17  |  Can't CONTINUE  |  The CONT command cannot be executed.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("18  |  Undefined user function  |  An attempt was made to use the user-defined function which has not been defined by DEF FN statement.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("19  |  Device I/O error  |  An error occurred in input/output of device.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("20  |  Verify error  |  The program on cassette and the one in memory are not the same.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("21  |  No RESUME  |  There is no RESUME statement in the error handling routine.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("22  |  RESUME without error  |  The RESUME statement is used other than in the error handling routine.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("23  |  Undefined.  |  ")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("24  |  Missing operand  |  Necessary parameters are not specified.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("25  |  Line buffer overflow  |  There are too many characters for the input data.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("26 to 49  |  Undefined.  |  ")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("50  |  FIELD overflow  |  The field size defined in FIELD statement exceeds 256 bytes.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("51  |  Internal error  |  An error occurred inside BASIC.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("52  |  Bad file number  |  File number which has not been OPENed is specified. The specified file number exceeds the number specified in MAXFILES statement.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("53  |  File not found  |  The specified file is not found.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("54  |  File already open  |  The file has already been OPENed.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("55  |  Input past end  |  The attempt to read the file is made after reading the end of it.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("56  |  Bad file name  |  There is an error in the specification of the file name.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("57  |  Direct statement  |  Data other than the program is found while loading the ASCII format program.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("58  |  Sequential I/O only  |  Random access to the sequential file is made.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("59  |  File not OPEN  |  The specified file has not been OPENed yet.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("60  |  Bad FAT  |  Unusual disk format.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("61  |  Bad file mode  |  An incorrect input/output operation is made in the OPENed mode.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("62  |  Bad drive name  |  There is an error in the drive name specification.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("63  |  Bad sector number  |  There is an error in the sector number.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("64  |  File still open  |  The file has not been closed.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("65  |  File already exists  |  The file name specified in NAME statement already exists on the disk.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("66  |  Disk full  |  The free area of the disk has been exhausted.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("67  |  Too many files  |  The number of files exceeds 112 (the directory space has been exhausted).")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("68  |  Disk write protected  |  The disk is protected from writing.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("69  |  Disk I/O error  |  Some trouble occurred in the disk input/output.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("70  |  Disk offline  |  The diskette is not in.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("71  |  Rename accross disk  |  NAME statement is done across different disks.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("72  |  File write protected  |  The file has the read-only attribute set.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("73  |  Directory already exists  |  The directory name specified in CALL MKDIR statement already exists.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("74  |  Directory not found  |  The specified directory is not found.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("75  |  RAM disk already exists  |  Attempt to create the DOS 2 RAM disk when it already exists is made.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("76 to 255  |  Undefined.  |  ")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("* **Note:** Errors with codes 72 to 75 are added from version 2 of MSX DISK-BASIC. In version 1 they are undefined.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("Use larger numbers first for user error definition.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_Commit("Error code list", "Chapter 2: BASIC")
  Th2HandbookHelp_AddAnchor("Chapter2#error-code-list", 165)

  Th2HandbookHelp_Begin()
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("- In description of REM statement, `[]` field has been added.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("- In description of SGN function, _" + Chr(34) + "Examines the sign and returns..." + Chr(34) + "_ has been changed to _" + Chr(34) + "Examines the sign of `` and returns..." + Chr(34) + "_")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("- Descriptions for MSX DISK-BASIC statements DSKI$ and DSKO$ have been added.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("- Descriptions for new commands on MSX DISK-BASIC version 2 have been added.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("- In [[[Table 2.20 (List of intermediate codes)|||Chapter2#table-220--list-of-intermediate-codes]]], the code " + Chr(34) + "FC" + Chr(34) + " is shown as assigned to " + Chr(34) + "\" + Chr(34) + " as it is actually, and not to " + Chr(34) + "$" + Chr(34) + " as in the original text.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("- In [[[List 2.3 (Changing error handling routine)|||Chapter2#list-23--changing-error-handling-routine]]], the third line of " + Chr(34) + "command initialize" + Chr(34) + ", which is " + Chr(34) + "LD HL,CMDHDAT" + Chr(34) + " in the original, is corrected to " + Chr(34) + "LD HL,HDAT" + Chr(34) + ".")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("- In [[[Section 5, " + Chr(34) + "Notes on Software Development" + Chr(34) + "|||Chapter2#5-notes-on-software-development]]], subsection " + Chr(34) + "BASIC version number" + Chr(34) + ", the part " + Chr(34) + "and so on" + Chr(34) + " has been added in point 1.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("- In [[[Error code list|||Chapter2#error-code-list]]], description of errors 72 to 75 have been added.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_Commit("Changes from the original", "Chapter 2: BASIC")
  Th2HandbookHelp_AddAnchor("Chapter2#changes-from-the-original", 166)

  Th2HandbookHelp_Begin()
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("Large capacity storage devices with high-speed access are necessary for business applications. That is why a disk operating system was added to the MSX machine. The DOS (disk operating system) is also required to handle the large amount of data on the disk effectively. MSX-DOS is derived from MS-DOS which is used widely on 16-bit machines. Thus, it represents the most powerful DOS environment for Z-80 based machines. Chapter 3 describes the basic operations of MSX-DOS and the use of the system calls.")
  Th2HandbookHelp_Commit("CHAPTER 3 - MSX-DOS", "Chapter 3: MSX-DOS")
  Th2HandbookHelp_AddAnchor("Chapter3#chapter-3---msx-dos", 167)

  Th2HandbookHelp_Begin()
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("[[[1.  OVERVIEW|||Chapter3#1--overview]]]")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("[[[1.1 Features of MSX-DOS|||Chapter3#11-features-of-msx-dos]]]")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("[[[1.2 MSX-DOS Environment|||Chapter3#12-msx-dos-environment]]]")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("[[[1.3 MSX-DOS System Resources|||Chapter3#13-msx-dos-system-resources]]]")
  Th2HandbookHelp_L("")
